⚡ Smart Meter Data Reconciliation & Audit Engine
An asynchronous, high-performance data processing web application built to ingest, validate, clean, and reconcile massive utility smart meter datasets (LP, DP, BP, SSR, NSC, MI, MDM, MDS, CP, SAT, FIT). Powered by FastAPI and DuckDB, this engine automates complex cross-dataset auditing, unpivots time-series records, and computes completion percentages with real-time UI progress updates across Windows, macOS, and Linux.

📌 Overview
Managing and reconciling millions of smart meter data records across disparate formats (Parquet files and date-wise nested CSV folders) is computationally intensive and prone to schema mismatches and cross-OS path incompatibilities.

This application streamlines the entire audit lifecycle into an automated 8-Stage Reconciliation Pipeline. By utilizing DuckDB's in-memory columnar execution, pathlib-based cross-platform path handling, and HTMX polling, it provides instant feedback during ingestion and audit computation, generating cleaned, downloadable reconciliation reports (final_lp.csv, final_dp.csv, and final_bp.csv).

⚡ Key Features
Cross-Platform Compatibility: Fully platform-agnostic architecture running seamlessly across Windows, macOS, and Linux using POSIX-normalized path resolution (pathlib.Path and .as_posix()).

High-Speed Columnar Ingestion: Process Parquet files and multi-folder datewise CSVs effortlessly using DuckDB's native file-reading capabilities (read_csv_auto, union_by_name=true, read_parquet).

Asynchronous Progress Tracking: Real-time progress bars and stage updates powered by HTMX polling and FastAPI BackgroundTasks.

8-Stage Reconciliation Pipeline:

Automated WFM (Workforce Management) base table construction from approved SSR, NSC, and MI records.

Multi-table exclusion indexing and filtering (SAT and FIT table validation).

Master list validation across MDM, MDS, and CP datasets.

Regex-based device serial number normalization (stripping ISK, LNT, and separator prefixes).

Dynamic date unpivoting (UNPIVOT) to calculate expected vs. received data ratios and completion percentages.

Metadata enrichment (including meter installation dates, network type, and communication hardware types like RF vs. Cellular).

Instant Export & Interactive Preview: Downloadable audit reports (LP, DP, BP) generated dynamically relative to application root, accompanied by interactive HTML data preview tables directly in the browser interface.

🛠️ Tech Stack
Backend Framework: FastAPI (Python)

SQL/Analytics Engine: DuckDB (In-memory OLAP Database)

Path & Environment Management: Python pathlib + os.path (POSIX Path Normalization)

Frontend UI & Interactivity: HTMX, Jinja2 Templates

Styling: Tailwind CSS

Concurrency: Python BackgroundTasks + Asyncio

🖥️ Cross-Platform Architecture Highlights
To ensure the application runs identically on any environment (local Windows desktops, macOS developer setups, Linux production servers, or Docker containers), the following core mechanisms are enforced:

Normalized POSIX SQL Paths: All user-provided string paths are normalized via Path(path).as_posix(). This translates OS-specific path formats (e.g., converting Windows C:\data\file backslashes into C:/data/file) so DuckDB’s underlying SQL engine reads files cleanly on all platforms.

Dynamic Project Root Resolution: File system outputs (COPY TO) and template locations rely on pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent instead of hardcoded drive letters or OS-dependent string concatenation.

OS-Safe File System Traversal: File search wildcards utilize os.path.join() combined with normalized folder paths to execute recursive wildcard globbing (*.csv, **/*.csv) reliably across both POSIX and Windows file systems.

🔄 8-Stage Audit Engine Pipeline
Stage 1 (Base Creation): Extracts approved records from SSR (Smart to Smart Replacement) to build the base WFM table.

Stage 2 (Record Merging): Ingests non-duplicate approved records from NSC (New Service Connection) and MI (Meter Installation).

Stage 3 & 4 (Exclusion Filtering): Creates indexed lookups on SAT and FIT tables to remove matched installed/tested records.

Stage 5 (Master Validation): Cross-validates remaining consumer and meter numbers against MDM, MDS, and CP master repositories.

Stage 6 (Prefix Cleaning): Strips hardware prefixes (ISK_, LNT-, etc.) using DuckDB regex functions across LP, DP, and BP datasets.

Stage 7 (Unpivoting & Ratios): Dynamically unpivots time-series date columns to calculate EXPECTED vs RECEIVED record counts and completion PERCENTAGE.

Stage 8 (Export & UI Delivery): Exports finalized datasets to root-relative CSV files (final_lp.csv, final_bp.csv, final_dp.csv) and renders styled preview tables directly to the UI.


